# Release signing material. Never commit these — an upload key in git means
# anyone with repo access can publish as this app.
/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Build-environment notes. Kept local: the file records this machine's disk
# layout, hardware, and what else runs on it, none of which belongs in a public
# repository. env.sh and sdk.sh carry everything a build actually needs.
/ENVIRONMENT.md

# Release runbook and risk register. Kept local for two reasons: the console
# steps only concern whoever publishes the build, and the risk section is an
# adverse analysis of this project's own naming — publishing your own "this may
# infringe" note helps nobody and can be quoted straight back at you.
/PLAY.md
